                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "workItemUris": [
            "GB-875"
          ],
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "prNoteAnchor/v1": "33292a1671bfc87e77caf7516ad45c58"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mscpyo0o68vrp9xj",
          "message": {
            "text": "The old engine is named by absolute path rather than letting openDataDir resolve it, because its default resolution would silently pick the wrong engine.\n\nopenDataDir tries the module specifier first and only downloads when it does not resolve at all — \"an installed engine wins\". The engine installed here is @electric-sql/pglite at the new major, which is precisely the one that cannot read this directory. Passing the default specifier would therefore resolve successfully and then fail on the first query with an opaque PGlite failed to initialize properly.\n\nPassing engine.entry from acquireEngine removes the ambiguity: the acquired PG17 build opens the PG17 directory, by construction.\n\nThis assumption depends on openDataDir keeping resolution-before-acquisition semantics. If a future pglite-migrate gains a force-acquire option, this could use it instead — but naming the engine explicitly stays correct either way.\n",
            "markdown": "The old engine is named by absolute path rather than letting `openDataDir` resolve it, because its default resolution would silently pick the wrong engine.\n\n`openDataDir` tries the module specifier first and only downloads when it does not resolve at all — \"an installed engine wins\". The engine installed here is `@electric-sql/pglite` at the *new* major, which is precisely the one that cannot read this directory. Passing the default specifier would therefore resolve successfully and then fail on the first query with an opaque `PGlite failed to initialize properly`.\n\nPassing `engine.entry` from `acquireEngine` removes the ambiguity: the acquired PG17 build opens the PG17 directory, by construction.\n\nThis assumption depends on `openDataDir` keeping resolution-before-acquisition semantics. If a future `pglite-migrate` gains a force-acquire option, this could use it instead — but naming the engine explicitly stays correct either way.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
